WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
San Juan Ermita plot. A computer voice is reading this.

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:14.509
In February, March and April, your land is usually left with no plants covering it. The satellite saw it from 2021 to 2025.

3
00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:20.960
In 2 of the last 15 years there were fires within half a kilometer of your plot, in March and April.

4
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:27.769
In 1 of the last 25 years, the midsummer drought brought more than 15 days in a row with almost no rain.

5
00:00:28.019 --> 00:00:41.028
This year, July and August got only a fifth of the normal rain (20 %). That is less than in 2018, the driest year since 1991. It is a preliminary figure.

6
00:00:41.278 --> 00:00:45.841
Today there are two even options: maize with jack bean or sorghum with cowpea.

7
00:00:46.091 --> 00:01:02.667
NASA computes 33 possible climates for 2041 to 2060. Planting as today, maize with beans has enough water in 5 of 33. Maize with jack bean: in 5. Sorghum with cowpea: in all 33.

8
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:06.790
This is not an official notice: talk it over with your extension worker.
